## 9. Refactoring OOP Code

Refactoring means improving the internal structure of existing code without changing its external behavior.

Common refactoring activities:

- Removing duplicate code.
- Splitting large classes.
- Improving method names.
- Reducing unnecessary dependencies.
- Simplifying complex methods.
- Improving readability.

**Goal:** Make code cleaner and easier to maintain without changing what the application does.

