## 10. Writing Maintainable Classes

Maintainable classes are easier to understand, modify, test, and extend.

### Best Practices

1. Give each class a clear responsibility.
2. Use meaningful class and method names.
3. Avoid unnecessarily large classes.
4. Keep methods focused.
5. Avoid unnecessary code duplication.
6. Reduce tight coupling.
7. Follow SOLID principles where appropriate.
8. Use composition when it gives a clearer design.
9. Validate input where necessary.
10. Write tests for important behavior.

