## 11. Inheritance vs Composition

### Inheritance

Inheritance represents an **IS-A** relationship.

A child class inherits and extends the behavior of a parent class.

Example:

```text
Dog IS-A Animal
```

### Composition

Composition represents a **HAS-A** relationship.

One object contains or owns another object as part of its functionality.

Example:

```text
Car HAS-A Engine
```

### Comparison

| Inheritance | Composition |
|---|---|
| Represents IS-A | Represents HAS-A |
| Uses parent-child relationships | Combines separate objects |
| Reuses behavior through inheritance | Reuses behavior through delegation |
| Can create tight coupling | Often provides greater flexibility |

**Best Practice:** Prefer composition over inheritance when it produces a simpler and more flexible design. Inheritance is appropriate when a genuine IS-A relationship exists.

